    "Real-surface regression samples are SIBLING STORY VARIANTS of the same component: two real renders that differ by content. They establish that separation exists at this scale; they do NOT establish a minimum detectable change, so no one may quote the regression figure as the smallest difference the gate can catch.",
    "Noise samples are two independent captures at stabilityRetries: 0. The production capture path defaults to retrying until byte-identical, so this figure is an UPPER bound on the variance a real comparison sees, not the variance it will see.",
